message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PHLAME: A Phase-Level Hardware-in-the-Loop Framework for Reproducible Fidelity-Ladder Evaluation of TinyML Image Classifiers on ARM Cortex-M Microcontrollers"
abstract: >-
  An open-source, reproducible framework for evaluating TinyML vision
  classifiers across the four-level MIL–SIL–PIL–HIL fidelity ladder on ARM
  Cortex-M7 microcontrollers (Arduino Portenta H7 + Vision Shield HM01B0).
  PHLAME couples deterministic dataset partitioning and INT8 post-training
  quantization with cycle-accurate DWT phase-level latency profiling
  (CAPTURE, PRE, INF, POST, TOTAL), on-chip FNV-1a model-identity
  verification, environmental condition tracking, and a camera-in-the-loop
  HIL bench that decomposes the simulation-to-hardware gap into quantization,
  on-chip execution, and optical-frontend effects.
